.TH "ANX" "1" "Oct 2026" "anx 1.0.0" "Anx User Manual"

.SH NAME
anx-capture - Ingest live dotfiles back into the repository with optional git commit & push


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBanx capture [group|config-id] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Capture live user dotfiles from $HOME back into the repository files/ directory.

.PP
Supports both rapid non-interactive execution and interactive interview wizard mode.
Optionally stages, commits to a feature branch, and pushes to git origin with strict
ownership verification (only allowed repository owners/members can push).


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-a\fP, \fB--all\fP[=true]
	Capture all supported configurations

.PP
\fB-b\fP, \fB--branch\fP=""
	Target git branch name (defaults to sync/dotfiles-)

.PP
\fB-c\fP, \fB--commit\fP[=false]
	Create a git commit on a feature branch

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for capture

.PP
\fB-m\fP, \fB--message\fP=""
	Commit message override

.PP
\fB-p\fP, \fB--push\fP[=false]
	Push the feature branch to remote origin (guard-protected)

.PP
\fB-w\fP, \fB--wizard\fP[=false]
	Interactive step-by-step review wizard


